# Build context for the Dockerfile, as an allowlist: everything is excluded,
# except what the Dockerfile copies. New files in the repo therefore never
# reach the builder unless they are added here explicitly.
#
# Purposes:
# - Keep local files (databases, secrets, .git, editor/agent folders) out of
#   the build context, so a careless COPY can never put them into the image.
#   The image itself only contains the binary.
# - Keep the local static/js/node_modules (macOS binaries) out: the frontend
#   stage installs its own Linux packages with npm ci, and COPY static would
#   otherwise copy the local ones over them.
# - Keep the build cache stable: changes to tests, coverage reports or docs
#   don't invalidate the build layers.

# Exclude everything, allow only what the Dockerfile copies
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!main.go
!backend/
!static/

# Exclude again inside the allowed folders (the last matching line wins, so
# these override !backend/ and !static/): tests, generated reports, local
# packages and build output, docs, the README-only logo
**/*_test.go
**/*.md
**/node_modules/
**/test-results/
**/.DS_Store
backend/testdata/
static/js/tests/
static/js/coverage/
static/js/vitest.config.js
static/dist/
static/logo.png
